**Summary of findings:**

1. **`App.tsx`** — Renders conditionally based on `status` (from `useAppInit`) and `modelsCount`. Statuses: `loading`, `no-workspace`, `cli-error`, `no-models`, `not-logged-in`, `ready`. The `SetupScreen` is shown when no API key is set (`!hasApiKey`) or `forceShowSetup` is true, but only when status is not `loading`, `cli-error`, or `no-workspace`.

2. **`useAppInit.ts`** — Defines `AppStatus = "loading" | "no-workspace" | "cli-error" | "not-logged-in" | "no-models" | "ready"`. The init flow: check workspace → get extension config, MCP servers, CLI check → check login status + get models → determine final status. Has a `refresh()` mechanism via `initKey` state.

3. **`WelcomeScreen.tsx`** — Simple component showing `ConsiliumLogo` + a hint (either a component or title/description). Used as the empty-state content inside `ChatArea`.

4. **`ConfigErrorScreen.tsx`** — Renders different error screens based on `type` prop (`loading`, `no-workspace`, `cli-error`, `no-models`). Each renders centered content with logo, icon, title, description, and action buttons. Uses internal `CLIErrorContent` and `NoModelsContent` sub-components.

5. **`bridge-handler.ts`** — The `BridgeHandler` class manages sessions, turns, custom work dirs, file manager, and active tabs. It handles RPC messages via `handle(msg, webviewId)`, dispatching to registered `handlers[method]`. Key methods: `getOrCreateSession` (creates/restarts sessions), `disposeView`/`dispose` (cleanup), `setCustomWorkDir`, `setSessionMetadata`/`getSessionMetadata`.

6. **`shared/types.ts`** — Contains all shared type definitions: `ExtensionConfig`, `CLICheckResult`, `LoginStatus`, `UIStreamEvent`, `AppStatus` (used in webview), `SessionMetadata`, `WorkspaceStatus`, etc.
